      "writtenOn": "2023-04-24T18:44:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like a lot of the code is done in the jni_thread instead of the main_thread. This looks wrong since we are cleaning native code.\n\nI would prefer the code to be updated to change this.",
      "parentUuid": "993d250a_626d0593",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "f7afa641d3dc65faaa7a55c13b090537f169f79f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2dcd8cb4_9b35a6e2",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1794306
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T07:58:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, one issue is that upstream is stack-\u003eJava, but cleanup is Java-\u003estack, so this makes they must be in the different thread ideally.\nAnother solution here is using a mutex to blocking the usage of callbacks.",
      "parentUuid": "e18ef8c2_4d3be64c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "f7afa641d3dc65faaa7a55c13b090537f169f79f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2210c8a2_43cd5405",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T21:16:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I understand we have this two possibility:\n* `do_in_main_thread` for java → stack\n* `do_in_jni_thread` for stack → java\n\nThis CL is about a java → stack call and you are adding a `do_in_jni_thread`\nIt\u0027s either:\n* not fixing the issue (since we are already from jni) \n* fixing it, meaning that \"multiple JNI thread are talking to the native\" ⇒ This would be a critical issue to address in priority.\n\n\nBut since we are in native stack, I do not think code should be executed in jni thread. Looking at `btif_hf.cc`, it is doing a lot of stuff in jni thread and that looks wrong.\nFor example the [transfer context](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/refs/heads/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/btif/src/btif_hf.cc;l\u003d710;drc\u003d7346c436e5a11ce08f6a80dcfeb8ef941ca30176) in `bte_hf_evt` looks really error-prone.\n\nPlease let me know what your think.\nI will let the area owner decide what he want to do with this but I feel like we are going in the wrong direction",
      "parentUuid": "2dcd8cb4_9b35a6e2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 37
      },
